(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[13] = [{"v":1,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"इदं शरीरं कौन्तेय क्षेत्रमित्यभिधीयते ।\nएतद्यो वेत्ति तं प्राहुः क्षेत्रज्ञ इति तद्विदः ॥","iast":"idaṃ śarīraṃ kaunteya kṣetramityabhidhīyate |\netadyo vetti taṃ prāhuḥ kṣetrajña iti tadvidaḥ ||","read":"idam shareeram kaunteya kshetramityabhidheeyate |\netadyo vetti tam praahuh kshetrajna iti tadvidah ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: This body, son of Kuntî, is called the Field; that which knoweth it is called the Knower of the Field by the Sages.","en2":"This body, O son of Kunti, is called Kshetra, and he who knows it is called Kshetrajna by those who know of them (Kshetra and Kshetrajna).","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"क्षेत्रज्ञं चापि मां विद्धि सर्वक्षेत्रेषु भारत ।\nक्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञयोर्ज्ञानं यत्तज्ज्ञानं मतं मम ॥","iast":"kṣetrajñaṃ cāpi māṃ viddhi sarvakṣetreṣu bhārata |\nkṣetrakṣetrajñayorjñānaṃ yattajjñānaṃ mataṃ mama ||","read":"kshetrajnam chaapi maam viddhi sarvakshetreshu bhaarata |\nkshetrakshetrajnayorjnaanam yattajjnaanam matam mama ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Understand Me as the Knower of the Field in all Fields, O Bhârata. Wisdom as to the Field and the Knower of the Field, that in My opinion is the wisdom.","en2":"Me do thou also know, O descendant of Bharata, to be Kshetrajna in all Kshetras. The knowledge of Kshetra and Kshetrajna is considered by Me to be the knowledge.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तत्क्षेत्रं यच्च यादृक्च यद्विकारि यतश्च यत् ।\nस च यो यत्प्रभावश्च तत्समासेन मे शृणु ॥","iast":"tatkṣetraṃ yacca yādṛkca yadvikāri yataśca yat |\nsa ca yo yatprabhāvaśca tatsamāsena me śṛṇu ||","read":"tatkshetram yachcha yaadrikcha yadvikaari yatashcha yat |\nsa cha yo yatprabhaavashcha tatsamaasena me shrinu ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"What that Field is and of what nature, how modified, and whence it is, and what He is and what His powers, hear that now briefly from Me.","en2":"What the Kshetra is, what its properties are, what are its modifications, what effects arise from what causes, and also who He is and what His powers are, that hear from Me in brief.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ऋषिभिर्बहुधा गीतं छन्दोभिर्विविधैः पृथक् ।\nब्रह्मसूत्रपदैश्चैव हेतुमद्भिर्विनिश्चितैः ॥","iast":"ṛṣibhirbahudhā gītaṃ chandobhirvividhaiḥ pṛthak |\nbrahmasūtrapadaiścaiva hetumadbhirviniścitaiḥ ||","read":"rishibhirbahudhaa geetam chhandobhirvividhaih prithak |\nbrahmasootrapadaishchaiva hetumadbhirvinishchitaih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Rishis have sung in manifold ways, in many various chants, and in decisive Brahma-sûtra verses full of reasonings.","en2":"(This truth) has been sung by Rishis in many ways, in various distinctive chants, in passages indicative of Brahman, full of reasoning, and convincing.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"महाभूतान्यहङ्कारो बुद्धिरव्यक्तमेव च ।\nइन्द्रियाणि दशैकं च पञ्च चेन्द्रियगोचराः ॥","iast":"mahābhūtānyahaṅkāro buddhiravyaktameva ca |\nindriyāṇi daśaikaṃ ca pañca cendriyagocarāḥ ||","read":"mahaabhootaanyahankaaro buddhiravyaktameva cha |\nindriyaani dashaikam cha pancha chendriyagocharaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The great Elements, Individuality, Reason, and also the unmanifested, the ten senses and the one, and the five pastures of the senses;","en2":"The great Elements, Egoism, Intellect, as also the Unmanifested (Mulâ Prakriti), the ten senses and the one (mind), and the five objects of the senses; desire, hatred, pleasure, pain, the, aggregate, intelligence, fortitude,—the Kshetra has been thus briefly described with its modifications.","en2r":"13.5-6","rv":null},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इच्छा द्वेषः सुखं दुःखं सङ्घातश्चेतनाधृतिः ।\nएतत्क्षेत्रं समासेन सविकारमुदाहृतम् ॥","iast":"icchā dveṣaḥ sukhaṃ duḥkhaṃ saṅghātaścetanādhṛtiḥ |\netatkṣetraṃ samāsena savikāramudāhṛtam ||","read":"ichchhaa dveshah sukham duhkham sanghaatashchetanaadhritih |\netatkshetram samaasena savikaaramudaahritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Desire, aversion, pleasure, pain, combination, intelligence, firmness; these, briefly described, constitute the Field and its modifications.","en2":"The great Elements, Egoism, Intellect, as also the Unmanifested (Mulâ Prakriti), the ten senses and the one (mind), and the five objects of the senses; desire, hatred, pleasure, pain, the, aggregate, intelligence, fortitude,—the Kshetra has been thus briefly described with its modifications.","en2r":"13.5-6","rv":null},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अमानित्वमदम्भित्वमहिंसा क्षान्तिरार्जवम् ।\nआचार्योपासनं शौचं स्थैर्यमात्मविनिग्रहः ॥","iast":"amānitvamadambhitvamahiṃsā kṣāntirārjavam |\nācāryopāsanaṃ śaucaṃ sthairyamātmavinigrahaḥ ||","read":"amaanitvamadambhitvamahimsaa kshaantiraarjavam |\naachaaryopaasanam shaucham sthairyamaatmavinigrahah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Humility, unpretentiousness, harmlessness, forgiveness, rectitude, service of the teacher, purity, steadfastness, self-control.","en2":"Humility, unpretentiousness, non-injury, forbearance, uprightness, service to the teacher, purity, steadiness, self-control;","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इन्द्रियार्थेषु वैराग्यमनहङ्कार एव च ।\nजन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिदुःखदोषानुदर्शनम् ॥","iast":"indriyārtheṣu vairāgyamanahaṅkāra eva ca |\njanmamṛtyujarāvyādhiduḥkhadoṣānudarśanam ||","read":"indriyaartheshu vairaagyamanahankaara eva cha |\njanmamrityujaraavyaadhiduhkhadoshaanudarshanam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Dispassion towards the objects of the senses, and also absence of egoism, insight into the pain and evil of birth, death, old age and sickness,","en2":"The renunciation of sense-objects, and also absence of egoism; reflection on the evils of birth, death, old age, sickness and pain;","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"असक्तिरनभिष्वङ्गः पुत्रदारगृहादिषु ।\nनित्यं च समचित्तत्वमिष्टानिष्टोपपत्तिषु ॥","iast":"asaktiranabhiṣvaṅgaḥ putradāragṛhādiṣu |\nnityaṃ ca samacittatvamiṣṭāniṣṭopapattiṣu ||","read":"asaktiranabhishvangah putradaaragrihaadishu |\nnityam cha samachittatvamishtaanishtopapattishu ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Unattachment, absence of self-identification with son, wife or home, and constant balance of mind in wished-for and unwished-for events,","en2":"Non-attachment, non-identification of self with son, wife, home, and the rest, and constant even-mindedness in the occurrence of the desirable and the un-undesirable;","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मयि चानन्ययोगेन भक्तिरव्यभिचारिणी ।\nविविक्तदेशसेवित्वमरतिर्जनसंसदि ॥","iast":"mayi cānanyayogena bhaktiravyabhicāriṇī |\nviviktadeśasevitvamaratirjanasaṃsadi ||","read":"mayi chaananyayogena bhaktiravyabhichaarinee |\nviviktadeshasevitvamaratirjanasamsadi ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Unflinching devotion to Me by yoga, without other objects, resort to sequestered places, absence of enjoyment in the company of men,","en2":"Unswerving devotion to Me by the Yoga of non-separation, resort to sequestered places, distaste for the society of men;","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अध्यात्मज्ञाननित्यत्वं तत्त्वज्ञानार्थदर्शनम् ।\nएतज्ज्ञानमिति प्रोक्तमज्ञानं यदतोन्यथा ॥","iast":"adhyātmajñānanityatvaṃ tattvajñānārthadarśanam |\netajjñānamiti proktamajñānaṃ yadatonyathā ||","read":"adhyaatmajnaananityatvam tattvajnaanaarthadarshanam |\netajjnaanamiti proktamajnaanam yadatonyathaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Constancy in the wisdom of the Self, understanding of the object of essential wisdom; that is declared to be the Wisdom; all against it is ignorance.","en2":"Constant application to spiritual knowledge, understanding of the end of true knowledge: this is declared to be knowledge, and what is opposed to it is ignorance.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ज्ञेयं यत्तत्प्रवक्ष्यामि यज्ज्ञात्वाऽमृतमश्नुते ।\nअनादिमत्परं ब्रह्म न सत्तन्नासदुच्यते ॥","iast":"jñeyaṃ yattatpravakṣyāmi yajjñātvā’mṛtamaśnute |\nanādimatparaṃ brahma na sattannāsaducyate ||","read":"jneyam yattatpravakshyaami yajjnaatvaa'mritamashnute |\nanaadimatparam brahma na sattannaasaduchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"I will declare that which ought to be known, that which being known immortality is enjoyed—the beginningless supreme Eternal, called neither being nor non-being.","en2":"I shall describe that which has to be known, knowing which one attains to immortality, the beginningless Supreme Brahman. It is called neither being nor non-being.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वतः पाणिपादं तत्सर्वतोऽक्षिशिरोमुखम् ।\nसर्वतः श्रुतिमल्लोके सर्वमावृत्य तिष्ठति ॥","iast":"sarvataḥ pāṇipādaṃ tatsarvato’kṣiśiromukham |\nsarvataḥ śrutimalloke sarvamāvṛtya tiṣṭhati ||","read":"sarvatah paanipaadam tatsarvato'kshishiromukham |\nsarvatah shrutimalloke sarvamaavritya tishthati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Everywhere That hath hands and feet, everywhere eyes, heads, and mouths; all-hearing, He dwelleth in the world, enveloping all,","en2":"With hands and feet everywhere, with eyes, heads and mouths everywhere, with ears everywhere in the universe,—That exists pervading all.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सर्वेन्द्रियगुणाभासं सर्वेन्द्रियविवर्जितम् ।\nअसक्तं सर्वभृच्चैव निर्गुणं गुणभोक्तृ च ॥","iast":"sarvendriyaguṇābhāsaṃ sarvendriyavivarjitam |\nasaktaṃ sarvabhṛccaiva nirguṇaṃ guṇabhoktṛ ca ||","read":"sarvendriyagunaabhaasam sarvendriyavivarjitam |\nasaktam sarvabhrichchaiva nirgunam gunabhoktri cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Shining with all sense-faculties without any senses; unattached supporting everything and free from qualities enjoying qualities;","en2":"Shining by the functions of all the senses, yet without the senses; Absolute, yet sustaining all; devoid of Gunas, yet their experiencer.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"बहिरन्तश्च भूतानामचरं चरमेव च ।\nसूक्ष्मत्वात्तदविज्ञेयं दूरस्थं चान्तिके च तत् ॥","iast":"bahirantaśca bhūtānāmacaraṃ carameva ca |\nsūkṣmatvāttadavijñeyaṃ dūrasthaṃ cāntike ca tat ||","read":"bahirantashcha bhootaanaamacharam charameva cha |\nsookshmatvaattadavijneyam doorastham chaantike cha tat ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Without and within all beings, immovable and also movable; by reason of His subtlety imperceptible; at hand and far away is That.","en2":"Without and within (all) beings; the unmoving and also the moving; because of Its subtlety incomprehensible; It is far and near.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अविभक्तं च भूतेषु विभक्तमिव च स्थितम् ।\nभूतभर्तृ च तज्ज्ञेयं ग्रसिष्णु प्रभविष्णु च ॥","iast":"avibhaktaṃ ca bhūteṣu vibhaktamiva ca sthitam |\nbhūtabhartṛ ca tajjñeyaṃ grasiṣṇu prabhaviṣṇu ca ||","read":"avibhaktam cha bhooteshu vibhaktamiva cha sthitam |\nbhootabhartri cha tajjneyam grasishnu prabhavishnu cha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Not divided amid beings, and yet seated distributively; that is to be known as the supporter of beings; He devours and He generates.","en2":"Impartible, yet It exists as if divided in beings: It is to be known as sustaining beings; and devouring, as well as generating (them).","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ज्योतिषामपि तज्ज्योतिस्तमसः परमुच्यते ।\nज्ञानं ज्ञेयं ज्ञानगम्यं हृदि सर्वस्य विष्ठितम् ॥","iast":"jyotiṣāmapi tajjyotistamasaḥ paramucyate |\njñānaṃ jñeyaṃ jñānagamyaṃ hṛdi sarvasya viṣṭhitam ||","read":"jyotishaamapi tajjyotistamasah paramuchyate |\njnaanam jneyam jnaanagamyam hridi sarvasya vishthitam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That, the Light of all lights, is said to be beyond darkness; Wisdom, the Object of Wisdom, by Wisdom to be reached, seated in the hearts of all.","en2":"The Light even of lights, It is said to be beyond darkness; Knowledge, and the One Thing to be known, the Goal of' knowledge, dwelling in the hearts of all.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"इति क्षेत्रं तथा ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं चोक्तं समासतः ।\nमद्भक्त एतद्विज्ञाय मद्भावायोपपद्यते ॥","iast":"iti kṣetraṃ tathā jñānaṃ jñeyaṃ coktaṃ samāsataḥ |\nmadbhakta etadvijñāya madbhāvāyopapadyate ||","read":"iti kshetram tathaa jnaanam jneyam choktam samaasatah |\nmadbhakta etadvijnaaya madbhaavaayopapadyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Thus the Field, Wisdom and the Object of Wisdom, have been briefly told. My devotee, thus knowing, enters into My Being.","en2":"Thus Kshetra, knowledge, and that which has to be known, have been briefly stated. Knowing this, My devotee is fitted for My state.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रकृतिं पुरुषं चैव विद्ध्यनादी उभावपि ।\nविकारांश्च गुणांश्चैव विद्धि प्रकृतिसंभवान् ॥","iast":"prakṛtiṃ puruṣaṃ caiva viddhyanādī ubhāvapi |\nvikārāṃśca guṇāṃścaiva viddhi prakṛtisaṃbhavān ||","read":"prakritim purusham chaiva viddhyanaadee ubhaavapi |\nvikaaraamshcha gunaamshchaiva viddhi prakritisambhavaan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Know thou that Matter and Spirit are both without beginning; and know thou also that modifications and qualities are all Matter-born.","en2":"Know thou that Prakriti and Purusha are both beginningless; and know thou also that all modifications and Gunas are born of Prakriti.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कार्यकारणकर्तृत्वे हेतुः प्रकृतिरुच्यते ।\nपुरुषः सुखदुःखानां भोक्तृत्वे हेतुरुच्यते ॥","iast":"kāryakāraṇakartṛtve hetuḥ prakṛtirucyate |\npuruṣaḥ sukhaduḥkhānāṃ bhoktṛtve heturucyate ||","read":"kaaryakaaranakartritve hetuh prakritiruchyate |\npurushah sukhaduhkhaanaam bhoktritve heturuchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Matter is called the cause of the generation of causes and effects; Spirit is called the cause of the enjoyment of pleasure and pain.","en2":"In the production of the body and the senses, Prakriti is said to be the cause; in the experience of pleasure and pain, Purusha is said to be the cause.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"पुरुषः प्रकृतिस्थो हि भुङ्क्ते प्रकृतिजान्गुणान् ।\nकारणं गुणसङ्गोऽस्य सदसद्योनिजन्मसु ॥","iast":"puruṣaḥ prakṛtistho hi bhuṅkte prakṛtijānguṇān |\nkāraṇaṃ guṇasaṅgo’sya sadasadyonijanmasu ||","read":"purushah prakritistho hi bhunkte prakritijaangunaan |\nkaaranam gunasango'sya sadasadyonijanmasu ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Spirit seated in Matter useth the qualities born of Matter; attachment to the qualities is the cause of his births in good and evil wombs.","en2":"Purusha seated in Prakriti, experiences the Gunas born of Prakriti; the reason of his birth in good and evil wombs is his attachment to the Gunas.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"उपद्रष्टाऽनुमन्ता च भर्ता भोक्ता महेश्वरः ।\nपरमात्मेति चाप्युक्तो देहेऽस्मिन्पुरुषः परः ॥","iast":"upadraṣṭā’numantā ca bhartā bhoktā maheśvaraḥ |\nparamātmeti cāpyukto dehe’sminpuruṣaḥ paraḥ ||","read":"upadrashtaa'numantaa cha bhartaa bhoktaa maheshvarah |\nparamaatmeti chaapyukto dehe'sminpurushah parah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Supervisor and permitter, supporter, enjoyer, the great Lord, and also the supreme Self; thus is styled in this body the supreme Spirit.","en2":"And the Supreme Purusha in this body is also called the Looker-on, the Permitter, the Supporter, the Experiencer, the Great Lord, and the Highest Self.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"य एवं वेत्ति पुरुषं प्रकृतिं च गुणैःसह ।\nसर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि न स भूयोऽभिजायते ॥","iast":"ya evaṃ vetti puruṣaṃ prakṛtiṃ ca guṇaiḥsaha |\nsarvathā vartamāno’pi na sa bhūyo’bhijāyate ||","read":"ya evam vetti purusham prakritim cha gunaihsaha |\nsarvathaa vartamaano'pi na sa bhooyo'bhijaayate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who thus knoweth Spirit and Matter with its qualities, in whatsoever condition he may be, he shall not be born again.","en2":"He who thus knows the Purusha and Prakriti together with the Gunas, whatever his life, is not born again.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ध्यानेनात्मनि पश्यन्ति केचिदात्मानमात्मना ।\nअन्ये सांख्येन योगेन कर्मयोगेन चापरे ॥","iast":"dhyānenātmani paśyanti kecidātmānamātmanā |\nanye sāṃkhyena yogena karmayogena cāpare ||","read":"dhyaanenaatmani pashyanti kechidaatmaanamaatmanaa |\nanye saamkhyena yogena karmayogena chaapare ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Some by meditation behold the Self in the self by the Self; others by the Sânkhya Yoga, and others by the Yoga of Action;","en2":"Some by meditation behold the Self in their own intelligence by the purified heart, others by the path of knowledge, others again by Karma Yoga.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अन्ये त्वेवमजानन्तः श्रुत्वाऽन्येभ्य उपासते ।\nतेऽपि चातितरन्त्येव मृत्युं श्रुतिपरायणाः ॥","iast":"anye tvevamajānantaḥ śrutvā’nyebhya upāsate |\nte’pi cātitarantyeva mṛtyuṃ śrutiparāyaṇāḥ ||","read":"anye tvevamajaanantah shrutvaa'nyebhya upaasate |\nte'pi chaatitarantyeva mrityum shrutiparaayanaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Others also, ignorant of this, having heard of it from others, worship; and these also cross beyond death, adhering to what they had heard.","en2":"Others again not knowing thus, worship as they have heard from others. [paragraph continues] Even these go beyond death, regarding what they have heard as the Supreme Refuge.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यावत्सञ्जायते किञ्चित्सत्त्वं स्थावरजङ्गमम् ।\nक्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञसंयोगात्तद्विद्धि भरतर्षभ ॥","iast":"yāvatsañjāyate kiñcitsattvaṃ sthāvarajaṅgamam |\nkṣetrakṣetrajñasaṃyogāttadviddhi bharatarṣabha ||","read":"yaavatsanjaayate kinchitsattvam sthaavarajangamam |\nkshetrakshetrajnasamyogaattadviddhi bharatarshabha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whatsoever creature is born immobile or mobile, know thou, O best of the Bhâratas, that it is from the union between the Field and the Knower of the Field.","en2":"Whatever being is born, the moving or the unmoving, O bull of the Bhâratas, know it to be from the union of Kshetra and Kshetrajna.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"समं सर्वेषु भूतेषु तिष्ठन्तं परमेश्वरम् ।\nविनश्यत्स्वविनश्यन्तं यः पश्यति स पश्यति ॥","iast":"samaṃ sarveṣu bhūteṣu tiṣṭhantaṃ parameśvaram |\nvinaśyatsvavinaśyantaṃ yaḥ paśyati sa paśyati ||","read":"samam sarveshu bhooteshu tishthantam parameshvaram |\nvinashyatsvavinashyantam yah pashyati sa pashyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Seated equally in all beings, the supreme Lord, unperishing within the perishing—he who thus seeth, he seeth.","en2":"He sees, who sees the Lord Supreme, existing equally in all beings, deathless in the dying.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"समं पश्यन्हि सर्वत्र समवस्थितमीश्वरम् ।\nन हिनस्त्यात्मनाऽऽत्मानं ततो याति परां गतिम् ॥","iast":"samaṃ paśyanhi sarvatra samavasthitamīśvaram |\nna hinastyātmanā’’tmānaṃ tato yāti parāṃ gatim ||","read":"samam pashyanhi sarvatra samavasthitameeshvaram |\nna hinastyaatmanaa''tmaanam tato yaati paraam gatim ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Seeing indeed everywhere the same Lord equally dwelling, he doth not destroy the Self, and thus treads the highest Path.","en2":"Since seeing the Lord equally existent everywhere, he injures not Self by self, and so goes to the highest Goal.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":29,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"प्रकृत्यैव च कर्माणि क्रियमाणानि सर्वशः ।\nयः पश्यति तथाऽऽत्मानमकर्तारं स पश्यति ॥","iast":"prakṛtyaiva ca karmāṇi kriyamāṇāni sarvaśaḥ |\nyaḥ paśyati tathā’’tmānamakartāraṃ sa paśyati ||","read":"prakrityaiva cha karmaani kriyamaanaani sarvashah |\nyah pashyati tathaa''tmaanamakartaaram sa pashyati ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"He who seeth that Matter verily performeth all actions, and that the Self is actionless, he seeth.","en2":"He sees, who sees that all actions are done by Prakriti alone and that the Self is actionless.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":30,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यदा भूतपृथग्भावमेकस्थमनुपश्यति ।\nतत एव च विस्तारं ब्रह्म सम्पद्यते तदा ॥","iast":"yadā bhūtapṛthagbhāvamekasthamanupaśyati |\ntata eva ca vistāraṃ brahma sampadyate tadā ||","read":"yadaa bhootaprithagbhaavamekasthamanupashyati |\ntata eva cha vistaaram brahma sampadyate tadaa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"When he perceiveth the diversified existence of beings as rooted in One, and spreading forth from it, then he reacheth the Eternal","en2":"When he sees the separate existence of all beings inherent in the One, and their expansion from That (One) alone, he then becomes Brahman.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":31,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अनादित्वान्निर्गुणत्वात्परमात्मायमव्ययः ।\nशरीरस्थोऽपि कौन्तेय न करोति न लिप्यते ॥","iast":"anāditvānnirguṇatvātparamātmāyamavyayaḥ |\nśarīrastho’pi kaunteya na karoti na lipyate ||","read":"anaaditvaannirgunatvaatparamaatmaayamavyayah |\nshareerastho'pi kaunteya na karoti na lipyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Being beginningless and without qualities, the imperishable supreme Self, though seated in the body, O Kaunteya, worketh not nor is affected.","en2":"Being without beginning and devoid of Gunas, this Supreme Self, immutable, O son of Kunti, though existing in the body neither acts nor is affected.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":32,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यथा सर्वगतं सौक्ष्म्यादाकाशं नोपलिप्यते ।\nसर्वत्रावस्थितो देहे तथाऽऽत्मा नोपलिप्यते ॥","iast":"yathā sarvagataṃ saukṣmyādākāśaṃ nopalipyate |\nsarvatrāvasthito dehe tathā’’tmā nopalipyate ||","read":"yathaa sarvagatam saukshmyaadaakaasham nopalipyate |\nsarvatraavasthito dehe tathaa''tmaa nopalipyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As the omnipresent ether is not affected, by reason of its subtlety, so seated everywhere in the body the Self is not affected.","en2":"As the all-pervading Akâsha, because of its subtlety, is not tainted, so the Self existent in the body everywhere is not tainted.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":33,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यथा प्रकाशयत्येकः कृत्स्नं लोकमिमं रविः ।\nक्षेत्रं क्षेत्री तथा कृत्स्नं प्रकाशयति भारत ॥","iast":"yathā prakāśayatyekaḥ kṛtsnaṃ lokamimaṃ raviḥ |\nkṣetraṃ kṣetrī tathā kṛtsnaṃ prakāśayati bhārata ||","read":"yathaa prakaashayatyekah kritsnam lokamimam ravih |\nkshetram kshetree tathaa kritsnam prakaashayati bhaarata ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"As the one sun illumineth the whole earth, so the Lord of the Field illumineth the whole Field, O Bhârata.","en2":"As the one sun illumines all this world, so does He who abides in the Kshetra, O descendant of Bharata, illumine the whole Kshetra.","en2r":null,"rv":null},{"v":34,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञयोरेवमन्तरं ज्ञानचक्षुषा ।\nभूतप्रकृतिमोक्षं च ये विदुर्यान्ति ते परम् ॥","iast":"kṣetrakṣetrajñayorevamantaraṃ jñānacakṣuṣā |\nbhūtaprakṛtimokṣaṃ ca ye viduryānti te param ||","read":"kshetrakshetrajnayorevamantaram jnaanachakshushaa |\nbhootaprakritimoksham cha ye viduryaanti te param ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"They who by the eyes of Wisdom perceive this difference between the Field and the Knower of the Field, and the liberation of beings from Matter they go to the Supreme.","en2":"They who thus with the eye of knowledge perceive the distinction between the Kshetra and the Kshetrajna, and also the emancipation from the Prakriti of beings, they go to the Supreme.","en2r":null,"rv":null}];
